---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
---

<Site
  title="Privacy"
  description="Vellum is strictly local: no account, no server, no telemetry, no relay. Here is exactly what runs where."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Nothing leaves<br /><em>your machine.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Vellum is a set of static files. Once they're loaded, everything happens on your computer.
        This page says exactly what that means.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="where-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2 id="where-h">What lives where</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="card lead">
          <h3>Your character</h3>
          <p class="small">
            Stored in your browser's local storage, and in your share link. The link carries its
            data in the address itself; it isn't stored on any server.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card lead">
          <h3>Your frames</h3>
          <p class="small">
            Frames you make stay in local storage on your machine. Export one as a file if you want
            to share it. Library frames are bundled into the app.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card lead">
          <h3>Your camera</h3>
          <p class="small">
            With face tracking on, Vellum reads webcam frames to find your face and discards them.
            No frame, image or face data is stored or sent.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card lead">
          <h3>Your controls</h3>
          <p class="small">
            Hotkeys go through OBS. The Stream Deck plugin and the HUD in OBS talk over your
            computer's loopback address, 127.0.0.1. Nothing connects through the internet.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="not-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2 id="not-h">What Vellum doesn't have</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>No accounts and no sign-in.</li>
        <li>No analytics or telemetry in the app.</li>
        <li>No relay or sync between players. Each player's Vellum stands alone.</li>
        <li>No uploads. The Frame Library grows by pull request, not by upload.</li>
        <li>No third-party scripts, fonts or models. Everything is served from vellumhud.com.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="check-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2 id="check-h">Check it yourself</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Open your browser's developer tools on the app and watch the Network tab while you play.
          After the first load, nothing is sent. The app is open source on{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/alxjrvs/vellum">GitHub</a>, so you can read every line.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Site>
